## SECTION 04 — THE DESIGN PROCESS / FROM STRUCTURE TO EXPERIENCE

This is one of the most important sections.

Implement a long scroll-pinned animation inspired by the architectural floor-plan transformation in the reference website.

The section should remain pinned while the user scrolls through a multi-stage visual sequence.

Suggested scroll duration: approximately 4000–5000px on desktop, adjusted through testing.

### Visual Sequence

Stage 01 — STRUCTURE

An almost empty architectural grid.

Only basic construction lines are visible.

Stage 02 — FOUNDATION

Primary shapes, boundaries, and layout structures are progressively drawn.

Stage 03 — COMPOSITION

More detailed elements emerge.

The layout begins to resemble an actual website interface.

Stage 04 — INTERACTION

Interactive components, navigation, buttons, interface states, and connection lines appear.

Stage 05 — REFINEMENT

Typography, colors, spacing, and detailed interface components are revealed.

Stage 06 — EXPERIENCE

The completed visual composition is revealed.

The result should communicate the transformation of an initial idea into a polished digital experience.

### Important Implementation Requirements

Use:

- GSAP ScrollTrigger.
- Scroll pinning.
- Scroll scrubbing.
- SVG path drawing.
- SVG masks.
- Layered visual compositions.
- Carefully synchronized animation timelines.

The animation must be directly controlled by scroll progress.

If the user stops scrolling, the animation must stop at its current state.

Scrolling backward must reverse the animation naturally.

Do not use a pre-rendered video as a substitute for this animation.

The architectural illustration must be composed of independently controllable elements.

