# 05. MOTION DESIGN SYSTEM

Motion design is a core feature of this project, not a decorative enhancement.

Build a reusable motion architecture.

## Required Technologies

- GSAP
- GSAP ScrollTrigger
- GSAP SplitText (if available through the appropriate license)
- Lenis
- SVG
- CSS Masks
- SVG Filters
- Canvas 2D
- Three.js or React Three Fiber only where justified

## Required Animation Types

1. Scroll-pinned sections.
2. Scroll-scrubbed timelines.
3. SVG stroke drawing.
4. Sketch-to-render transitions.
5. Organic ink image reveals.
6. Split-word text animations.
7. Staggered grid reveals.
8. Image masking.
9. Subtle parallax.
10. Interactive cursor.
11. Custom hover interactions.
12. Interactive typography.
13. Section transitions.
14. Progressive architectural illustrations.
15. Smooth reverse animations when scrolling upward.

## Animation Principles

Every animation must have a clear visual purpose.

Use:

- Carefully controlled easing.
- Natural acceleration and deceleration.
- Smooth transitions.
- Appropriate stagger intervals.
- Consistent animation durations.
- Scroll progress synchronization.

Avoid:

- Random floating animations.
- Excessive bounce effects.
- Generic fade-in on every element.
- Unnecessary 3D transformations.
- Constant movement that distracts from content.
- Long animations that make the website feel unresponsive.

The result must feel deliberate, premium, and professionally art-directed.

